1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,879
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,845
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

7
00:01:12,948 --> 00:01:13,949
Thanks.

8
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:20,204
These photos...

9
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:21,540
They're the victims.

10
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:24,084
Jo Nayeong.

11
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:26,753
Choi Yeongmin.

12
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:31,758
Kim Heejun.

13
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:37,513
Jo Nayeong and Choi Yeongmin
were amateur models,

14
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:40,183
and they went missing the day
after they met Yu Seongwon.

15
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,145
So I was watching Yu Seongwon.

16
00:01:44,146 --> 00:01:45,856
SEPTEMBER 14, 2021

17
00:01:51,153 --> 00:01:52,237
[knock on car window]

18
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:55,240
You're a detective, right?

19
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:58,160
Can I get in?

20
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:08,003
What did Seongwon do?

21
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,296
Why do you ask?

22
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:11,922
Because I'm curious.

23
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:14,425
I'm really close with him.
[inhales sharply]

24
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:15,801
But how should I put this?

25
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:18,179
Sometimes he seems a little crazy.

26
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:21,183
The other day, while having a drink,
he said something strange.

27
00:02:22,476 --> 00:02:23,559
What did he say?

28
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:27,939
That he wanted to use
a corpse as his model.

29
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:31,651
He said if the model moves
while he's feeling inspired,

30
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:32,736
he wants to kill them.

31
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:36,740
I heard his models disappeared.

32
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:38,450
Is it true?

33
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,080
Can I have your number?

34
00:02:51,004 --> 00:02:52,838
GANGHA POLICE
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

35
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:55,092
I'll let you know
if he does anything suspicious.

36
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:56,760
Wait.

37
00:02:57,803 --> 00:03:00,222
It's too dangerous. Stay away from him.

38
00:03:01,098 --> 00:03:03,349
I've got good instincts.

39
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,476
I'll keep you updated.

40
00:03:10,107 --> 00:03:11,858
[Hyera] <i>Kim Heejun
went missing after that.</i>

41
00:03:13,402 --> 00:03:14,986
<i>And Yu Seongwon moved to the UK.</i>

42
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:22,953
I believe Yu Seongwon made that piece
after killing Kim Heejun,

43
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:29,418
to put his murder on display.

44
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,922
He wants to show off

45
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,508
that he's the killer.

46
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:41,138
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

47
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,399
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

48
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,778
I couldn't pinpoint
where the other victims had been murdered,

49
00:03:59,114 --> 00:04:01,323
but Kim Heejun likely died
in a field of reeds.

50
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:03,325
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

51
00:04:03,326 --> 00:04:05,035
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

52
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:07,247
He left a clue in his artwork on purpose.

53
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:10,666
Because he's become certain
he'd never get caught.

54
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,918
[Isoo sighs softly]

55
00:04:13,128 --> 00:04:14,670
DALSEONG WETLAND

56
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:17,174
YEONGSAN RIVER GARDEN

57
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,176
Is that why you collected these?

58
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:21,260
[Hyera] Yes.

59
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:22,344
GAPCHEON WETLAND

60
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:24,681
I need to find out
where the murder happened

61
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:28,018
to at least recover the body.

62
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,606
Will you help me?

63
00:04:41,615 --> 00:04:43,617
[♪ tense, suspenseful music continues]

64
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:52,793
EPISODE 9

65
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:01,134
[Isoo sighs softly]

66
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,182
[chuckles] Young Master.

67
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:11,143
Gosh, you're still calling me
"Young Master."

68
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:13,270
Have you been well? It's been a while.

69
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,898
It's good to see you again.

70
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,982
Seongwon is inside, isn't he?

71
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:19,026
Yes. Please go ahead.

72
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,987
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

73
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:48,598
[Seongwon] Oh!

74
00:05:49,391 --> 00:05:50,392
Isoo!

75
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,478
Hey, what are you doing here?
You didn't even call.

76
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:55,689
I was just passing by.

77
00:05:56,857 --> 00:05:58,692
You missed me, didn't you? [chuckles]

78
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,819
What's that? A gift?

79
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,070
Yeah.

80
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:05,490
It's the whiskey I made.

81
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:08,702
Wait here a second.

82
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,996
Mr. Hwang!

83
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:12,955
Do we have any fruit?

84
00:06:12,956 --> 00:06:15,208
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

85
00:06:45,196 --> 00:06:46,280
[♪ music fades]

86
00:06:46,281 --> 00:06:47,324
[exhales contentedly]

87
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:50,868
Wow. Did you really make this?

88
00:06:50,869 --> 00:06:52,620
Of course I did.

89
00:06:52,621 --> 00:06:54,330
This is a work of art.

90
00:06:54,331 --> 00:06:55,414
- Cheers.
- [chuckles]

91
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:56,750
[clink]

92
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,255
By the way, that piece there.

93
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:04,132
What does it mean?

94
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,467
[Seongwon] Mmm?

95
00:07:06,468 --> 00:07:09,012
[Isoo] What's with the pebbles
and why stick the reed in?

96
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:12,098
I just don't get it.

97
00:07:14,893 --> 00:07:15,976
Why do you ask?

98
00:07:15,977 --> 00:07:17,936
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

99
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,272
It's a secret.

100
00:07:24,486 --> 00:07:25,569
You...

101
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:28,489
[exclaims incredulously] You're acting
like I know nothing about art again.

102
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,699
Forget it. Don't tell me
if you don't want to.

103
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,284
[chuckles] No, it's fine.

104
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,703
I'll make an exception for you.

105
00:07:35,038 --> 00:07:36,414
[Seongwon] Mmm...

106
00:07:40,502 --> 00:07:41,961
For me,

107
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:45,507
there are moments I could never forget.

108
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,470
Moments I can recall
down to every last detail.

109
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:53,807
The sunlight that day,

110
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:56,476
the smell of the air,

111
00:07:57,686 --> 00:07:59,437
it's all in my head.

112
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,027
The moment I first met you is one of them.

113
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:08,113
[♪ music fades]

114
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:09,739
Me?

115
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:12,575
At the gathering?

116
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:17,747
You don't remember, do you?

117
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:21,000
We met way before that.

118
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,419
When I was just a kid.

119
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,213
I've liked you ever since then.

120
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:29,884
That piece

121
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,928
is a memory of one of those moments.

122
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,013
[♪ ominous music playing]

123
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:36,975
In a field of reeds in early winter,

124
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:41,396
I'm walking forward,
stepping over the gravel.

125
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,905
It was drizzling that day.

126
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:00,915
[Heejun] Seongwon.

127
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,196
I made that piece to remember that moment.

128
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:43,541
[♪ music fades]

129
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,672
I met Seongwon yesterday.

130
00:09:50,757 --> 00:09:51,758
What do you think?

131
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,885
I don't know if he's the real killer,

132
00:09:54,886 --> 00:09:55,887
but here.

133
00:09:58,098 --> 00:09:59,723
I took it from that sculpture.

134
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:00,850
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

135
00:10:04,479 --> 00:10:05,647
By the way,

136
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:08,983
there was a kiln in his studio.

137
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:12,737
A kiln?

138
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:16,615
If he burned the bodies there...

139
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,243
We won't find any DNA.

140
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:21,537
[sighs]

141
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:23,039
I'll look into this first.

142
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:24,749
Also,

143
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:28,128
he said it was raining that day.

144
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,506
The day he found inspiration
for that piece.

145
00:10:32,507 --> 00:10:33,842
[♪ music swells]

146
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:38,471
[♪ music fades]

147
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,558
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

148
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:56,614
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

149
00:11:03,955 --> 00:11:07,584
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
MOON SEYEON

150
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:14,548
[♪ music fades]

151
00:11:14,549 --> 00:11:16,301
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

152
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,099
[blade swooshing]

153
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,042
[♪ music stops]

154
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,252
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

155
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,136
[♪ music turns ominous]

156
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:07,352
[♪ music swells, fades]

157
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:09,020
[exhales softly]

158
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,190
[sniffles]

159
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:18,695
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

160
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:20,198
[blade swooshing]

161
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:44,472
[♪ music turns suspenseful]

162
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,977
[panting]

163
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:53,022
[girl, weakly] Please... help me.

164
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:55,984
[♪ ominous music playing]

165
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:05,034
[sword clatters]

166
00:13:08,371 --> 00:13:09,746
[Seyeon] Don't come any closer.

167
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,707
Stay away from me!

168
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,709
[screaming]

169
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:15,252
Go away!

170
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:16,545
[♪ music swells, fades]

171
00:13:16,546 --> 00:13:17,714
[scream echoes, fades]

172
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:25,179
[students chattering]

173
00:13:36,566 --> 00:13:37,567
DANCE STUDIO 1

174
00:13:39,986 --> 00:13:41,153
[all scream]

175
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:42,738
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

176
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:43,740
Oh, my God.

177
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:46,324
[students whispering anxiously]

178
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:47,784
Why aren't you girls going in?

179
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:48,828
[student] Ms. Jeong.

180
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:51,164
What?

181
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,045
[♪ music increases in tempo]

182
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:01,006
[Juhee gasps]

183
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,216
[♪ music swells]

184
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:04,760
[♪ music fades]

185
00:14:04,761 --> 00:14:06,637
[siren blaring]

186
00:14:11,642 --> 00:14:12,810
[brakes squeal]

187
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:14,812
[siren stops blaring]

188
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,622
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

189
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,715
- [Isoo] How did this happen?
- [♪ music fades]

190
00:14:43,716 --> 00:14:45,801
Let's check if anyone's been in or out.

191
00:14:45,802 --> 00:14:46,803
Got it.

192
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:56,104
[sighs softly]

193
00:14:58,356 --> 00:14:59,899
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

194
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:05,278
- [audio distorts]
- [slow, muffled thuds]

195
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:07,406
[high-pitched tone droning, intensifies]

196
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:11,034
- [high-pitched tone fades]
- [audio normalizes]

197
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:12,578
[♪ soft melancholy music continues]

198
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:21,796
Please have a look.

199
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,592
[dispenser clicks]

200
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,136
[exhales heavily]

201
00:15:33,391 --> 00:15:35,768
[Isoo breathing heavily]

202
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:41,315
[Hyera] What's wrong?

203
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:45,153
[panting] Uh...

204
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,405
I was just thirsty.

205
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:50,074
[exhales heavily]

206
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:53,035
- [continues panting]
- [♪ music fades]

207
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:55,037
[knock at door]

208
00:15:57,456 --> 00:15:59,207
We're from Gangha Police Station.

209
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:00,793
Who is the deceased student?

210
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:03,795
Her name is Moon Seyeon.

211
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:04,964
I'm her homeroom teacher.

212
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:08,425
When did you last see her?

213
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:09,551
Uh...

214
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:10,927
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

215
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,471
When school let out at 5:00 p.m.

216
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:14,139
But

217
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,018
she said she was going to rehearse
in the practice room from 9:00.

218
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,020
Nine o'clock at night?

219
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,604
Yes.

220
00:16:20,605 --> 00:16:23,024
Is the practice room
used at night as well?

221
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,025
Uh...

222
00:16:25,026 --> 00:16:27,485
Seyeon is the lead dancer
in the arts festival,

223
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:29,821
so she was allowed to use it anytime.

224
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:30,990
Allowed by whom?

225
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:33,618
The principal.

226
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:38,122
Seyeon was personally instructed
by the principal.

227
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:42,500
Do the teachers stay late
at school with her?

228
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,545
No, we go home for the day.

229
00:16:45,296 --> 00:16:48,841
The principal sometimes stays behind
to help Seyeon with practice,

230
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,468
but she left early yesterday.

231
00:16:51,469 --> 00:16:54,512
Then who is at school late at night?

232
00:16:54,513 --> 00:16:56,849
The security guard on night duty.

233
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:00,143
- Check with the security office.
- [both] Okay.

234
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,021
[♪ music swells, fades]

235
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:08,276
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

236
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:10,070
GRAND PRIZE

237
00:17:10,071 --> 00:17:12,114
AWARD CERTIFICATE

238
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:16,494
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

239
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:20,664
[♪ music fades]

240
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:21,666
[knock at door]

241
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:24,293
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

242
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:26,963
[Isoo] We're from Gangha Police Station.

243
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:29,090
[gasps]

244
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,092
PRINCIPAL OF JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
JEONG JOOHEE

245
00:17:32,093 --> 00:17:33,928
Aren't you the dancer Jeong Joohee?

246
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:37,055
You know me?

247
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,599
Of course. I even went
to your performance in New York.

248
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,018
It's an honor.

249
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:43,521
[chuckles softly]

250
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,022
She's famous.

251
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:48,233
A living legend of Korean dance.

252
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:50,945
[chuckles softly] You're too kind.
It's all in the past.

253
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:54,573
This is my team leader.
She doesn't get out much.

254
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:58,327
- She knows nothing about the arts.
- I'm Joo Hyera with Gangha Police.

255
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,453
Uh, I'm Jin Isoo.

256
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:01,747
Right, yes.

257
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,541
Please have a seat.

258
00:18:04,125 --> 00:18:05,418
[Isoo exhales in awe]

259
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:08,044
CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT

260
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:10,798
Oh, so you became a principal.

261
00:18:11,382 --> 00:18:13,717
I had some health issues.

262
00:18:13,718 --> 00:18:16,511
Now I devote my time to teaching students.

263
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:19,264
Oh. They're lucky
to be learning from a legend.

264
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:20,932
[chuckles softly] Not at all.

265
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,560
I appreciate your kind words.

266
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:27,188
We're here because of Moon Seyeon.
You know what happened, right?

267
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:28,898
[breath trembles] Yes.

268
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,150
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

269
00:18:30,151 --> 00:18:31,152
[exhales heavily]

270
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,696
I was so shocked
at the studio this morning.

271
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:37,241
We heard you personally instructed Seyeon.

272
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:40,828
She was a very talented student.

273
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:44,957
She had the potential
to become a great dancer.

274
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:48,084
Was Seyeon at school
by herself last night?

275
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,169
[Juhee] Yes.

276
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,964
She was scheduled
to practice on her own yesterday.

277
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:54,507
The arts festival is
just around the corner,

278
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:57,428
so she worked very hard,
practicing every day without fail.

279
00:18:58,679 --> 00:19:00,680
[Hyera breathes deeply]

280
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:04,517
Was there anyone
who didn't get along with Seyeon?

281
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,228
Teacher or student, anyone at all.

282
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:07,855
I'm not sure.

283
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,815
She wasn't a difficult person,

284
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,568
and she was an outgoing, sweet girl.

285
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,362
She was the lead dancer of the festival,

286
00:19:15,363 --> 00:19:18,239
and she was personally taught by you.

287
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,242
Someone might have been jealous of her.

288
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:23,161
That happens all the time.

289
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,248
All my students
are ambitious and passionate.

290
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:30,335
Being jealous and competitive
is part of how you grow, isn't it?

291
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,670
That's true.

292
00:19:31,671 --> 00:19:34,090
But killing someone for that reason?

293
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:36,759
There's no one like that at our school.

294
00:19:40,054 --> 00:19:41,137
[♪ music fades]

295
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:43,098
I was on duty yesterday.

296
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:45,767
I went home this morning,
but came back after I got the call.

297
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:48,645
Did you see
the deceased student last night?

298
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:52,273
Yes, she came in around 9:00 p.m.

299
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:54,235
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

300
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,366
<i>She's been coming every night.</i>

301
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:03,243
Did you notice anything unusual?

302
00:20:03,244 --> 00:20:04,577
Like anyone following her?

303
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:07,998
No, she went inside
and I locked the gate right away.

304
00:20:10,835 --> 00:20:12,377
Was that the last time you saw her?

305
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:15,171
I last saw her
when I was making my round at 10:00 p.m.

306
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:16,965
She was practicing alone.

307
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:19,051
[♪ muffled percussive folk music plays]

308
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,642
Did you notice anything unusual then?

309
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:28,643
Like I said, no.

310
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:31,271
Did you check inside all the classrooms?

311
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:34,357
Well, not really,
but all the classrooms were locked.

312
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:37,570
There really was no one there.
I have no idea how this happened.

313
00:20:39,155 --> 00:20:40,197
[♪ music fades]

314
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,949
Could you copy
all the security footage onto this?

315
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:43,951
[softly] Sure.

316
00:20:46,454 --> 00:20:48,371
What's going to happen to me?

317
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:49,832
Will I get in trouble for this?

318
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:52,042
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

319
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:55,378
Why would you worry about that?

320
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:59,341
I'm just worried
I might get blamed for this.

321
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:02,511
You'll be fine
if you've done nothing wrong.

322
00:21:03,471 --> 00:21:04,555
[sighs wearily]

323
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:14,189
CHANGING ROOM

324
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,483
[♪ music swells]

325
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:21,739
[♪ music fades]

326
00:21:22,364 --> 00:21:24,575
- Let's visit the victim's home first.
- Okay.

327
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:26,951
Oh.

328
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:28,496
- Mmm. Delicious.
- [Isoo] It's <i>bungeoppang.</i>

329
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,247
I've wanted to try that.

330
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,665
Have you never had <i>bungeoppang?</i>

331
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:34,334
They don't sell it near my place.

332
00:21:34,335 --> 00:21:36,921
- [chuckles softly] Go get some.
- Really?

333
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:38,714
Nice!

334
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:41,508
- Be quick.
- Okay, got it.

335
00:21:41,509 --> 00:21:42,593
Where do you buy those?

336
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:44,929
Where's Isoo going?

337
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,721
To get <i>bungeoppang.</i>

338
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,349
- He's never had it before.
- What?

339
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:51,684
[scoffs] He surprisingly hasn't tried
a lot of things.

340
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:53,645
What did the security guard say?

341
00:21:53,646 --> 00:21:56,231
He last saw her
while making his rounds at 10:00 p.m.

342
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:58,067
He didn't see anyone suspicious.

343
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,695
[breathes deeply]

344
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,739
- There you go.
- [students] Thank you.

345
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,907
- [vendor] Bye.
- Hello.

346
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:06,991
[♪ jaunty music playing]

347
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:08,117
[softly] Oh...

348
00:22:08,118 --> 00:22:09,619
PIZZA, SPICY

349
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:10,913
LOW SUGAR CUSTARD, RED BEAN

350
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:13,874
Excuse me, what's the "custard" flavor?

351
00:22:14,667 --> 00:22:16,417
It's filled with custard cream.

352
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:17,710
Oh!

353
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:20,296
Then I'll take four of each flavor.

354
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:22,132
Coming right up.

355
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:26,261
NO CARD, CASH ONLY
BANK TRANSFER DETAILS

356
00:22:26,262 --> 00:22:28,179
Don't you take card?

357
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:29,639
You can pay by bank transfer.

358
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,808
- Bank transfer?
- [vendor] Yes.

359
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:32,852
Bank transfer.

360
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:34,936
[♪ music fades]

361
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:37,355
I'm sure Moon Seyeon died
because of the curse.

362
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,899
[student] That curse was real.

363
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:41,734
You think that girl really killed her?

364
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,736
Why else did she die in the practice room?

365
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:44,738
What do you mean?

366
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:46,782
A curse?

367
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:49,492
- Girls.
- Here, all packed up for you.

368
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:51,912
- Please transfer the money.
- Right, bank transfer.

369
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:54,122
Girls!

370
00:22:54,123 --> 00:22:56,250
Don't go.
I'll buy you custard <i>bungeoppang!</i>

371
00:22:56,584 --> 00:22:57,585
[sighs]

372
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,131
By the way,

373
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:04,841
the students said something weird.

374
00:23:04,842 --> 00:23:06,176
Like what?

375
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,678
That Seyeon died from a curse.

376
00:23:08,679 --> 00:23:10,722
- A curse?
- [Isoo] Yeah.

377
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:13,224
They said she was cursed
and died in the practice room.

378
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:15,144
- Really?
- Yeah.

379
00:23:20,024 --> 00:23:21,025
Mmm.

380
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:22,526
Personally,

381
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:26,571
I prefer red bean.

382
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:28,364
[♪ jaunty music playing]

383
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:30,074
I'm trying to be serious here.

384
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,161
- I prefer custard.
- [Kyungjin, muffled] I prefer red bean.

385
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:35,080
Really?

386
00:23:36,957 --> 00:23:38,082
[♪ music fades]

387
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,085
SEWON HOSPITAL

388
00:23:43,756 --> 00:23:45,423
[footsteps approaching]

389
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:46,633
[Dr. Jinkyung] Hello.

390
00:23:46,634 --> 00:23:47,842
[chuckles]

391
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,385
It's been a while.

392
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:50,387
Hello.

393
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:52,639
Did you have chemotherapy?

394
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:53,891
- Yes.
- [chuckles softly]

395
00:23:54,892 --> 00:23:56,684
How are you feeling?

396
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,978
Much better, thanks to you.

397
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,313
I'm glad to hear that.

398
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:03,358
I thought you were sitting here
because you weren't feeling well.

399
00:24:03,359 --> 00:24:04,818
I was just

400
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:09,322
thinking I might live
a little differently from now on.

401
00:24:09,323 --> 00:24:11,033
Differently? In what way?

402
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:16,162
I originally planned to retire
last year and travel the world.

403
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:17,498
Travel the world?

404
00:24:18,082 --> 00:24:20,416
It's nothing grand,

405
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:23,211
but I've only ever
traveled abroad for work.

406
00:24:23,212 --> 00:24:24,295
[♪ melancholy music playing]

407
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:26,297
Ah, you must've led quite a busy life.
[chuckles]

408
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:27,299
[chuckles]

409
00:24:27,925 --> 00:24:29,343
Traveling the world.

410
00:24:30,427 --> 00:24:31,679
That sounds nice.

411
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:35,224
I'm actually starting
my sabbatical next month.

412
00:24:36,058 --> 00:24:39,227
I was thinking of taking a trip, too.

413
00:24:39,228 --> 00:24:40,729
Sabbatical?

414
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:42,648
That's nice.

415
00:24:43,774 --> 00:24:47,277
I can't even remember the last time
I did nothing and just relaxed.

416
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:51,323
[sighs deeply] Time really flies,
doesn't it? [chuckles]

417
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:54,368
- It does.
- [chuckles]

418
00:24:59,707 --> 00:25:01,250
[♪ melancholy music continues]

419
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:10,968
[breath trembles] My daughter

420
00:25:12,219 --> 00:25:14,763
got divorced when Seyeon was little,

421
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:18,308
then passed away young.

422
00:25:20,728 --> 00:25:23,439
So I raised Seyeon on my own.

423
00:25:26,025 --> 00:25:28,359
[sniffles, breathes deeply]

424
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:31,946
She was such a sweet and lovely girl.

425
00:25:31,947 --> 00:25:35,074
Ever since she was little,
whenever she heard any music,

426
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:38,829
she would dance beautifully
like a fairy, like an angel.

427
00:25:41,290 --> 00:25:43,584
She said she'd become a famous dancer...

428
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:48,672
[voice shaking] ...and take good care
of her grandma. [sobbing]

429
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:56,055
As her grandmother, I had no money,

430
00:25:56,847 --> 00:25:58,265
no power.

431
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:02,019
[sniffles]
Even though that poor child was sick,

432
00:26:02,811 --> 00:26:05,439
she worked part-time
while going to school.

433
00:26:08,108 --> 00:26:10,778
Was she unwell?

434
00:26:11,737 --> 00:26:13,696
She had asthma.

435
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:15,574
[breath trembling]

436
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:19,327
But she still went to practice every day

437
00:26:19,328 --> 00:26:22,121
and even got the lead role
in the arts festival.

438
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:23,957
How could this happen? [sobbing]

439
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:33,050
Could we look around Seyeon's room?

440
00:26:34,218 --> 00:26:35,219
Yes.

441
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:47,481
- [continues sobbing]
- [door opens]

442
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,152
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

443
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:02,788
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

444
00:27:05,541 --> 00:27:07,209
AWARD CERTIFICATE

445
00:27:26,103 --> 00:27:27,604
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

446
00:27:28,105 --> 00:27:29,188
Look at this.

447
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:30,691
[♪ music increases in tempo]

448
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:35,696
Is this the curse?

449
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:44,453
[Hyera] Do you know what this is?

450
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:45,497
What's this?

451
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:49,042
It was in her desk drawer.

452
00:27:49,710 --> 00:27:51,460
[Grandma, gasps shakily] Did someone

453
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:55,299
hate my granddaughter this much?

454
00:27:55,799 --> 00:27:57,676
[sobbing] Why?

455
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:00,888
[♪ music swells]

456
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:09,979
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

457
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:11,064
[♪ music fades]

458
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:16,153
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

459
00:28:16,778 --> 00:28:17,779
[Kyungjin] Hey!

460
00:28:18,655 --> 00:28:20,365
[laughing maniacally]

461
00:28:26,038 --> 00:28:27,121
What's with him?

462
00:28:27,122 --> 00:28:29,582
[Kyungjin continues laughing maniacally]

463
00:28:29,583 --> 00:28:31,083
His girlfriend dumped him.

464
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,460
[in English] What?

465
00:28:32,461 --> 00:28:34,129
Apparently,
it's a first for him.

466
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:36,965
[in Korean] How did a dating expert
get dumped?

467
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:38,884
Nobody

468
00:28:39,635 --> 00:28:41,470
- can bat a thousand.
- [cell phone vibrating]

469
00:28:43,305 --> 00:28:44,514
[Isoo exhales deeply]

470
00:28:46,767 --> 00:28:47,935
Hello, Jiwon?

471
00:28:49,645 --> 00:28:50,937
[♪ music fades]

472
00:28:50,938 --> 00:28:53,065
- Did something happen?
- No, it's nothing.

473
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:55,651
- Did you find anything?
- Not yet.

474
00:28:56,276 --> 00:28:59,154
I played it back from 9:00 p.m.,
but no one went into the building.

475
00:29:00,072 --> 00:29:02,074
[Isoo] You need to look carefully,
Kyungjin.

476
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:05,911
Our suspect is hiding deep in the shadows.

477
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,412
What?

478
00:29:08,497 --> 00:29:10,539
Remember the Han Yura case? The candles.

479
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:11,541
The candles.

480
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:13,835
The key to this case is the curse.

481
00:29:14,628 --> 00:29:17,463
A vengeful presence might've been
caught on camera. Play it.

482
00:29:17,464 --> 00:29:18,674
[scoffs softly]

483
00:29:22,511 --> 00:29:23,636
[keyboard clacking]

484
00:29:23,637 --> 00:29:25,097
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

485
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:32,937
Okay, I'll call you later.

486
00:29:32,938 --> 00:29:34,314
[♪ music fades]

487
00:29:34,982 --> 00:29:36,065
When's the autopsy?

488
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,943
They're just starting now.

489
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,654
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

490
00:29:48,495 --> 00:29:50,414
[Dr. Yoon, sighs] One second.

491
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:53,250
[camera shutter clicking]

492
00:29:55,711 --> 00:29:57,504
[♪ music increases in tempo]

493
00:30:10,434 --> 00:30:11,767
Do we have a time of death?

494
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:14,021
Between 10:00 and 11:00 p.m.

495
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:16,690
[sighs heavily]

496
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:19,860
Then we can't rule out the security guard.

497
00:30:20,902 --> 00:30:22,236
[both gasp]

498
00:30:22,237 --> 00:30:23,529
[♪ music fades]

499
00:30:23,530 --> 00:30:24,655
[Isoo gasps softly]

500
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:26,615
- Did you see that?
- Yes.

501
00:30:26,616 --> 00:30:28,201
What is it now?

502
00:30:29,745 --> 00:30:32,164
It's real.

503
00:30:32,706 --> 00:30:34,248
Here, look.

504
00:30:34,249 --> 00:30:36,043
[♪ ominous music playing]

505
00:30:36,501 --> 00:30:38,128
See? Right here.

506
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:41,672
Three, two, one.

507
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:43,090
[♪ ominous sting]

508
00:30:43,091 --> 00:30:44,301
[♪ music fades]

509
00:30:44,885 --> 00:30:45,927
[Isoo exhales sharply]

510
00:30:47,137 --> 00:30:48,220
[sniffles]

511
00:30:48,221 --> 00:30:49,473
It's probably a reflection.

512
00:30:50,140 --> 00:30:52,475
Yeah, like the shadow of a tree.

513
00:30:52,476 --> 00:30:54,351
How is this the shadow of a tree?

514
00:30:54,352 --> 00:30:58,022
- It's dust. There's dust on the camera.
- Yeah, she's right.

515
00:30:58,023 --> 00:31:00,357
Hey, what kind of ghost
shows up on camera?

516
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:03,611
Don't you know about spirit photography?
What kind of dust is that big?

517
00:31:03,612 --> 00:31:06,155
This looks way too much like a person.

518
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:07,615
That's enough.

519
00:31:07,616 --> 00:31:09,617
I don't know
how that got caught on camera,

520
00:31:09,618 --> 00:31:12,704
but no ghost or curse can kill a person.

521
00:31:13,371 --> 00:31:14,830
How can you be so sure?

522
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:17,124
The truth is out there.

523
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:18,877
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

524
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:24,800
Someone's vengeful spirit

525
00:31:25,634 --> 00:31:27,260
is haunting the school.

526
00:31:28,929 --> 00:31:29,930
A haunted arts school.

527
00:31:30,639 --> 00:31:32,474
[breath trembling, grunts]

528
00:31:33,934 --> 00:31:35,059
I'm scared.

529
00:31:35,060 --> 00:31:36,393
[♪ music fades]

530
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:37,395
[gasps softly]

531
00:31:38,188 --> 00:31:39,523
Is it really dust?

532
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:43,901
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

533
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:46,947
You found this inside Seyeon's desk?

534
00:31:48,156 --> 00:31:49,490
[exhales in disbelief]

535
00:31:49,491 --> 00:31:50,991
Who would do such a thing?

536
00:31:50,992 --> 00:31:53,620
Someone despised Moon Seyeon.

537
00:31:54,830 --> 00:31:56,164
Does anyone come to mind?

538
00:31:56,957 --> 00:31:58,124
[exhales softly]

539
00:31:58,125 --> 00:32:00,502
[breathes deeply] I really don't know.

540
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:06,091
Mmm, then do you know
who Seyeon's closest friend was?

541
00:32:09,594 --> 00:32:11,512
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

542
00:32:11,513 --> 00:32:13,639
[Hyera] We heard you were close to Seyeon.

543
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,307
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
PARK DAHYE

544
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,518
We had something to ask you.

545
00:32:17,644 --> 00:32:18,645
Okay.

546
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,608
This was inside Seyeon's desk.

547
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:26,360
[♪ music fades]

548
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:27,821
Who do you think sent it?

549
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,031
Anyone come to mind?

550
00:32:33,326 --> 00:32:35,787
You can be honest. It'll stay between us.

551
00:32:38,248 --> 00:32:41,125
There was an accident a week ago.

552
00:32:41,126 --> 00:32:42,501
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

553
00:32:42,502 --> 00:32:44,545
- An accident?
- [Dahye] Yes.

554
00:32:44,546 --> 00:32:47,424
Hayun fell and broke her arm.

555
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:50,384
[grunts, groans]

556
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:51,511
[whimpers]

557
00:32:55,182 --> 00:32:57,641
[groans, breathes heavily]

558
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:59,769
[Dahye] <i>I heard that Seyeon was behind it.</i>

559
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:02,521
Did Seyeon really push her?

560
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:04,441
She said it wasn't her,

561
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,568
but apparently, everyone saw it.

562
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,573
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
KIM HAYUN

563
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:15,368
Hayun, can you show us your arm?

564
00:33:19,623 --> 00:33:20,749
You're hurt.

565
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,335
How did that happen?

566
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:25,212
I just fell.

567
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,338
We heard Seyeon pushed you.

568
00:33:27,339 --> 00:33:28,840
Is that why you sent this to her?

569
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:30,842
What's this?

570
00:33:33,511 --> 00:33:34,763
I don't do stuff like this.

571
00:33:35,347 --> 00:33:37,056
Is it true that Seyeon pushed you?

572
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:38,515
Yes.

573
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:39,935
Why did she do it?

574
00:33:41,394 --> 00:33:43,938
She can't even dance,
but she got cocky about getting the lead,

575
00:33:43,939 --> 00:33:44,981
so I said something.

576
00:33:45,607 --> 00:33:46,690
What did you say?

577
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,984
I asked if she'd bribed the principal.

578
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:50,111
What do you mean?

579
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,198
There were always rumors about that.

580
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:56,201
About how the principal's
obsessed with money.

581
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,203
If she wasn't paid off,

582
00:33:58,954 --> 00:34:00,872
why would she pick Seyeon to be the lead?

583
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,793
This wasn't me.

584
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:09,923
Song Gaeun's the one
who'd do something so immature.

585
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:13,593
She's the one who really hated Seyeon.

586
00:34:16,429 --> 00:34:17,805
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
SONG GAEUN

587
00:34:17,806 --> 00:34:18,931
[Isoo] Try opening it.

588
00:34:18,932 --> 00:34:20,433
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

589
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:25,021
It was you.

590
00:34:26,982 --> 00:34:28,649
Why did you send this?

591
00:34:28,650 --> 00:34:30,026
Because I was pissed off.

592
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:32,946
Based on talent, I should be the lead.

593
00:34:35,198 --> 00:34:37,534
But this is just something everyone does.

594
00:34:38,159 --> 00:34:40,996
Do you think the principal favored Seyeon?

595
00:34:41,621 --> 00:34:42,789
Isn't that obvious?

596
00:34:43,665 --> 00:34:45,207
She really wasn't talented.

597
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:46,459
Why would she favor Seyeon?

598
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,086
How would I know?

599
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,839
But Seyeon told me

600
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:54,300
the principal has no choice
but to pick her for the lead.

601
00:34:54,301 --> 00:34:56,219
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

602
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:05,185
In any case,
this case has nothing to do with me.

603
00:35:05,186 --> 00:35:07,355
She didn't die because of this note.

604
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:12,193
Why did you write that you curse her?
People don't usually say that.

605
00:35:12,861 --> 00:35:13,945
And what's this paper?

606
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:17,531
I bought it at the Witch's Shop.

607
00:35:17,532 --> 00:35:19,242
It's a trend at school.

608
00:35:20,035 --> 00:35:21,036
Because of Baek Yuna.

609
00:35:21,786 --> 00:35:22,870
Baek Yuna?

610
00:35:22,871 --> 00:35:24,747
An upperclassman
who killed herself last year.

611
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:26,874
Someone killed herself here?

612
00:35:26,875 --> 00:35:29,668
Yes, in the practice room.

613
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:32,839
That's why all the girls are saying
that Baek Yuna killed Seyeon.

614
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:35,717
Were they connected somehow?

615
00:35:36,343 --> 00:35:37,677
I wouldn't know.

616
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:41,306
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

617
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:49,356
[camera shutter clicking]

618
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:54,402
[♪ music increases in tempo]

619
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:07,790
[forensics officer] What is all this?

620
00:36:07,791 --> 00:36:09,625
[♪ music swells, fades]

621
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:11,293
VICTIM, CRIME SCENE, PRACTICE ROOM

622
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:13,922
We responded to the scene
in the Baek Yuna case.

623
00:36:15,507 --> 00:36:17,759
Was that the ghost of Baek Yuna?

624
00:36:19,052 --> 00:36:20,261
Ghost?

625
00:36:21,513 --> 00:36:22,514
At this school,

626
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:26,101
Baek Yuna's ghost is
still wandering around.

627
00:36:26,685 --> 00:36:28,310
What's wrong with you?

628
00:36:28,311 --> 00:36:29,813
How did she die?

629
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:31,730
It was a suicide.

630
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:34,441
She cut an artery
in the practice room late at night.

631
00:36:34,442 --> 00:36:35,609
[♪ tense music playing]

632
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,444
Any chance it was a murder?

633
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:39,948
No one was on site
except the security guard.

634
00:36:40,323 --> 00:36:42,658
Ah, and the practice room was locked.

635
00:36:42,659 --> 00:36:44,034
What about security cameras?

636
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:45,786
That's the problem.

637
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:47,246
They were down.

638
00:36:47,247 --> 00:36:49,456
Why did she commit suicide?

639
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:50,624
[inhales deeply]

640
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:52,252
That's also a bit unclear,

641
00:36:52,961 --> 00:36:56,839
but she was on antidepressants
a month or two before the incident.

642
00:36:56,840 --> 00:36:57,966
Having said that,

643
00:36:58,967 --> 00:37:01,553
she did text her mother
before committing suicide.

644
00:37:02,137 --> 00:37:03,262
It said she was sorry.

645
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:04,305
MOM, I'M SORRY

646
00:37:05,265 --> 00:37:07,934
Were there rumors
that the principal was taking bribes?

647
00:37:09,477 --> 00:37:11,187
Yes, there were.

648
00:37:11,855 --> 00:37:14,189
The principal used to be a famous dancer,

649
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:17,484
but she quit because of a slipped disc
and returned to her old school.

650
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:21,071
There was talk that she loved
designer goods and bribes.

651
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:23,949
How is that related to Baek Yuna's case?

652
00:37:23,950 --> 00:37:25,951
We looked into it.

653
00:37:25,952 --> 00:37:27,244
According to the rumors,

654
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:30,080
Baek Yuna's mother was the one
who bribed the principal.

655
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:33,375
Baek Yuna's mother bribed the principal?

656
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:34,377
Wait,

657
00:37:35,044 --> 00:37:37,963
she became the lead of the festival
after bribing the principal

658
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:40,467
and had a promising future,
so why did she kill herself?

659
00:37:45,472 --> 00:37:46,555
[♪ music fades]

660
00:37:46,556 --> 00:37:48,474
"I curse you."

661
00:37:48,475 --> 00:37:50,726
I CURSE YOU

662
00:37:50,727 --> 00:37:52,270
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

663
00:37:53,646 --> 00:37:55,147
Was that about Seyeon?

664
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:56,900
VICTIM, MOON SEYEON, AGE 18

665
00:37:58,777 --> 00:38:00,820
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

666
00:38:02,822 --> 00:38:03,823
[forensics officer] Detective Joo.

667
00:38:06,785 --> 00:38:08,787
I found something strange.

668
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:12,957
We're still investigating
the contents that were inside.

669
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:18,670
I bought it at the Witch's Shop.

670
00:38:18,671 --> 00:38:20,215
It's a trend at school.

671
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:22,299
We need to meet this witch.

672
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:23,510
[♪ music fades]

673
00:38:30,767 --> 00:38:32,936
- [toy skeleton chimes]
- Jesus Christ!

674
00:38:38,775 --> 00:38:40,067
What on earth?

675
00:38:40,068 --> 00:38:41,903
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

676
00:38:44,656 --> 00:38:46,156
[owner, in deep voice] Welcome.

677
00:38:46,157 --> 00:38:48,993
OWNER OF THE WITCH'S SHOP
MA HYUNYOUNG

678
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:53,456
Do you wish to curse someone?

679
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:56,083
Or know the future?

680
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:59,253
In this place, you can do it all.

681
00:38:59,254 --> 00:39:01,256
- [clip clicks]
- We're police.

682
00:39:02,549 --> 00:39:05,801
[in normal voice] Gosh,
what brings the police here? [chuckles]

683
00:39:05,802 --> 00:39:09,597
Everything in here might look strange,
but it's just the shop's theme.

684
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:13,600
They're all just toys. Like this.

685
00:39:13,601 --> 00:39:15,018
[♪ quirky music playing]

686
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:17,605
A student from
Juyeon Arts High School recently died.

687
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:21,109
This was among her belongings.

688
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,152
How did she die?

689
00:39:24,153 --> 00:39:26,321
- We're still investigating that.
- [♪ music fades]

690
00:39:26,322 --> 00:39:28,532
- What is this?
- That's...

691
00:39:28,533 --> 00:39:30,492
It's just a way to blow off some steam.

692
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:31,494
It's really nothing.

693
00:39:34,664 --> 00:39:37,666
Uh, is this a real bone?

694
00:39:37,667 --> 00:39:38,917
[scoffs]

695
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:42,170
Oh, of course not. It's plastic.
Where would I get real bones?

696
00:39:42,171 --> 00:39:43,548
Yeah, I thought as much.

697
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:46,550
But do students buy a lot of this stuff?

698
00:39:46,551 --> 00:39:48,970
Business isn't exactly booming,

699
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:53,056
but a lot of Juyeon Arts students
have been coming since last year.

700
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:56,019
They buy curse charms
and protective charms.

701
00:39:56,603 --> 00:39:57,686
Mmm.

702
00:39:57,687 --> 00:39:58,980
I'll buy one of these, too.

703
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:00,607
Sure.

704
00:40:05,278 --> 00:40:06,321
Excuse me.

705
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:09,532
I need a copy
of your shop's security footage.

706
00:40:10,867 --> 00:40:12,035
[Hyunuong] Sure.

707
00:40:15,830 --> 00:40:17,248
Sorry, but...

708
00:40:17,916 --> 00:40:18,917
this is

709
00:40:19,876 --> 00:40:22,045
my fifth store.

710
00:40:23,671 --> 00:40:26,256
I really can't afford
to go out of business. [chuckles]

711
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:28,842
You should try changing your theme.

712
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:32,804
You're too sweet-looking
for a gloomy place like this.

713
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:34,056
[♪ quirky music playing]

714
00:40:34,057 --> 00:40:35,974
- Should I?
- [Isoo] Yes.

715
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:39,603
This "Good Luck" charm.
I'll buy ten of these.

716
00:40:39,604 --> 00:40:40,771
[gasps]

717
00:40:40,772 --> 00:40:44,024
Gosh, my Flex Cop! [squeals]

718
00:40:44,025 --> 00:40:46,151
- [Isoo] You know me?
- [Hyunuong] Of course I do.

719
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:48,070
There's no other chaebol this handsome.

720
00:40:48,071 --> 00:40:50,531
Can you sign your autograph here, too?

721
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:53,450
- On this?
- It's a curse charm. My bad.

722
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:54,952
[Isoo] Seriously, on a curse charm?

723
00:40:54,953 --> 00:40:56,329
[Hyunuong] I can't let you get cursed.

724
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:59,748
- I need a pen.
- Right, a pen. [giggles]

725
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:00,750
[Isoo, softly] Honestly.

726
00:41:03,419 --> 00:41:05,254
[♪ music fades]

727
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:08,382
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL D-6

728
00:41:08,383 --> 00:41:12,053
I know you're all having a hard time
after what happened to Seyeon.

729
00:41:13,638 --> 00:41:14,681
However,

730
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:17,892
the arts festival
must go ahead as planned.

731
00:41:18,601 --> 00:41:20,603
It's also the right thing
to do for Seyeon.

732
00:41:21,270 --> 00:41:24,856
So you must pull yourselves together
and keep practicing.

733
00:41:24,857 --> 00:41:26,025
[all] Yes, ma'am.

734
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:29,487
You know who's coming
to the festival, don't you?

735
00:41:30,113 --> 00:41:31,822
Deans from arts colleges,

736
00:41:31,823 --> 00:41:34,574
and even the Minister
of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

737
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:36,744
Your futures depend on this.

738
00:41:38,413 --> 00:41:39,956
The lead dancer will be...

739
00:41:40,748 --> 00:41:42,166
[♪ suspenseful piano music playing]

740
00:41:58,516 --> 00:41:59,559
...Song Gaeun.

741
00:42:05,565 --> 00:42:07,108
[♪ music turns ominous]

742
00:42:08,151 --> 00:42:09,693
You can do it, right, Gaeun?

743
00:42:09,694 --> 00:42:11,070
Yes, ma'am.

744
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:16,783
[♪ music fades]

745
00:42:16,784 --> 00:42:19,162
NATIONAL FORENSIC SERVICE

746
00:42:22,832 --> 00:42:24,042
[exhales sharply]

747
00:42:27,795 --> 00:42:29,422
[muttering]

748
00:42:34,052 --> 00:42:35,386
Jiwon!

749
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:37,638
What are you doing?

750
00:42:38,598 --> 00:42:39,931
Oh.

751
00:42:39,932 --> 00:42:41,600
Experimenting.

752
00:42:41,601 --> 00:42:42,685
What?

753
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:45,730
Ah...

754
00:42:46,522 --> 00:42:47,647
Look at this.

755
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:49,609
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

756
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:53,613
These wounds

757
00:42:54,197 --> 00:42:55,948
don't look like cuts from a blade.

758
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:58,659
The skin tore when the blade struck her.

759
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:02,955
This is the same kind of blade
the victim used.

760
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:08,294
The edge isn't sharp.

761
00:43:09,629 --> 00:43:10,879
The blade didn't cut her.

762
00:43:10,880 --> 00:43:13,382
It struck her and tore her skin.

763
00:43:14,050 --> 00:43:17,135
But the angle seemed a little odd,

764
00:43:17,136 --> 00:43:18,721
so I was trying it out myself.

765
00:43:19,514 --> 00:43:20,515
See?

766
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:23,726
It looks the same, right?

767
00:43:27,897 --> 00:43:29,397
Uh...

768
00:43:29,398 --> 00:43:31,192
- Then...
- Yes.

769
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:35,196
She did this to herself.

770
00:43:36,114 --> 00:43:37,365
Given the angle,

771
00:43:38,491 --> 00:43:39,574
it was self-inflicted.

772
00:43:39,575 --> 00:43:41,410
- [blunt thudding]
- [screaming]

773
00:43:45,748 --> 00:43:48,709
Can someone die from wounds like these?

774
00:43:49,335 --> 00:43:50,336
No.

775
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:52,922
<i>The victim had asthma.</i>

776
00:43:53,548 --> 00:43:57,176
<i>An asthma attack narrowed her airways,
which deprived her of oxygen.</i>

777
00:43:57,802 --> 00:43:59,428
<i>That led to cardiac arrest.</i>

778
00:44:01,889 --> 00:44:06,309
Also, we found
an unidentified metabolite in her blood,

779
00:44:06,310 --> 00:44:09,147
but we need to look into that further.

780
00:44:10,064 --> 00:44:11,189
Okay.

781
00:44:11,190 --> 00:44:12,358
[♪ music swells]

782
00:44:14,902 --> 00:44:16,112
[♪ music fades]

783
00:44:18,573 --> 00:44:20,199
PARK JUNYOUNG
INCOMING CALL

784
00:44:23,119 --> 00:44:24,786
[Junyoung, over car audio] <i>Hey, are you
with Detective Joo?</i>

785
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:26,163
Yes, go ahead.

786
00:44:26,164 --> 00:44:27,914
The autopsy results are out.

787
00:44:27,915 --> 00:44:30,458
She went into cardiac arrest
from an asthma attack.

788
00:44:30,459 --> 00:44:31,835
[Isoo] What?

789
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:33,461
What about the cuts on her legs?

790
00:44:33,462 --> 00:44:36,424
They seem self-inflicted.

791
00:44:37,216 --> 00:44:39,259
She did that to herself? Why?

792
00:44:39,260 --> 00:44:40,635
[Junyoung] <i>I don't know,</i>

793
00:44:40,636 --> 00:44:44,015
<i>but the angle suggests
she struck herself and the skin tore.</i>

794
00:44:44,599 --> 00:44:48,101
They also found an unusual metabolite.
They'll analyze it and let us know.

795
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:50,353
Okay, great job.

796
00:44:50,354 --> 00:44:51,397
Okay.

797
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:53,191
[Hyera] <i>Wait, Detective Park.</i>

798
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:56,818
Can you check Baek Yuna's case again?

799
00:44:56,819 --> 00:45:00,030
Start with the security guard.
The security cameras keep bothering me.

800
00:45:00,031 --> 00:45:02,033
- [Junyoung] <i>Okay, got it.
-</i> [line disconnects]

801
00:45:02,617 --> 00:45:05,535
Did Baek Yuna really curse Moon Seyeon?

802
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:06,954
[♪ tense music playing]

803
00:45:09,123 --> 00:45:11,708
Turn the car around.
I need to see the principal.

804
00:45:11,709 --> 00:45:13,585
What am I, your chauffeur?

805
00:45:13,586 --> 00:45:14,878
You can turn around there.

806
00:45:14,879 --> 00:45:18,048
Yes, ma'am, all right.

807
00:45:18,049 --> 00:45:19,382
[engine revs]

808
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:20,592
[♪ music fades]

809
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:22,552
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

810
00:45:22,553 --> 00:45:23,596
[Juhee] Yuna...

811
00:45:25,306 --> 00:45:26,933
was such a promising student.

812
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:31,645
You don't know how heartbroken I was
when she died like that.

813
00:45:31,646 --> 00:45:34,565
Why would she have taken her own life?

814
00:45:35,358 --> 00:45:37,026
I don't know.

815
00:45:38,027 --> 00:45:40,987
She did seem a little depressed
from before the incident,

816
00:45:40,988 --> 00:45:43,783
but no matter how much I asked,
she wouldn't tell me.

817
00:45:45,576 --> 00:45:47,662
We heard there were rumors

818
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:50,748
that Baek Yuna's mother gave you a bribe.

819
00:45:51,415 --> 00:45:52,540
[sighs wearily]

820
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:54,751
[inhales] That's a misunderstanding.

821
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:57,045
It was a donation for the arts festival,

822
00:45:57,046 --> 00:46:00,090
but people who like to gossip
spread those ridiculous rumors.

823
00:46:00,091 --> 00:46:01,300
What about Seyeon?

824
00:46:02,843 --> 00:46:06,222
The students believe
you received a bribe from her.

825
00:46:06,806 --> 00:46:08,307
[sighs softly, inhales]

826
00:46:08,933 --> 00:46:11,310
They're too young to know any better.

827
00:46:12,019 --> 00:46:13,062
You see, Seyeon

828
00:46:13,771 --> 00:46:15,647
came from a low-income family.

829
00:46:15,648 --> 00:46:17,524
She also had asthma,

830
00:46:17,525 --> 00:46:20,194
so she had a hard time
practicing with the other students.

831
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:22,821
She had a lot of potential,

832
00:46:22,822 --> 00:46:25,115
so I picked her as the lead dancer

833
00:46:25,116 --> 00:46:27,076
and allowed her to practice on her own.

834
00:46:32,957 --> 00:46:35,583
What happened to Seyeon?

835
00:46:35,584 --> 00:46:37,795
It seems she died from an asthma attack.

836
00:46:38,379 --> 00:46:40,005
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

837
00:46:40,006 --> 00:46:42,174
We came to tell you
that this wasn't a murder.

838
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:44,175
[exhales sharply]

839
00:46:44,176 --> 00:46:47,721
Then what happened to her legs?

840
00:46:47,722 --> 00:46:49,472
[Isoo] Mmm.

841
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:50,474
That

842
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:54,020
might be Baek Yuna's curse.

843
00:46:54,687 --> 00:46:57,564
Uh, this is just my unofficial opinion.

844
00:46:57,565 --> 00:46:58,858
What are you talking about?

845
00:46:59,442 --> 00:47:01,860
[inhales sharply] This school

846
00:47:01,861 --> 00:47:04,530
is filled with the energy of a curse.

847
00:47:10,161 --> 00:47:11,203
Uh...

848
00:47:11,954 --> 00:47:12,955
What's this?

849
00:47:13,956 --> 00:47:15,333
Have you never seen it before?

850
00:47:16,167 --> 00:47:17,877
It's a trend among the students.

851
00:47:18,419 --> 00:47:19,836
It's a curse pouch.

852
00:47:19,837 --> 00:47:21,921
The students carry this around?

853
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:23,382
No.

854
00:47:24,342 --> 00:47:26,344
They secretly slip the curse in.

855
00:47:27,386 --> 00:47:29,722
My gosh, how could they do such a thing?

856
00:47:34,602 --> 00:47:35,603
[exhales softly]

857
00:47:37,188 --> 00:47:38,814
[♪ music increases in tempo]

858
00:47:52,078 --> 00:47:53,745
[♪ music turns ominous]

859
00:47:53,746 --> 00:47:55,498
SONG GAEUN

860
00:48:00,920 --> 00:48:02,296
[intercom chimes]

861
00:48:05,800 --> 00:48:06,883
Oh.

862
00:48:06,884 --> 00:48:09,220
I'm with Gangha Police.
You remember me, right?

863
00:48:09,929 --> 00:48:11,096
Yes.

864
00:48:11,097 --> 00:48:13,265
May I come in for a second?

865
00:48:13,974 --> 00:48:14,975
Sure.

866
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:24,735
Did I do something wrong?

867
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:30,657
Uh, a student died
at school last fall, right?

868
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:31,951
Yes.

869
00:48:32,701 --> 00:48:33,744
Back then,

870
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:39,249
- why did you do it?
- What?

871
00:48:39,250 --> 00:48:41,085
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

872
00:48:42,795 --> 00:48:44,004
Why did you do it?

873
00:48:53,305 --> 00:48:55,181
Because I was scared.

874
00:48:55,182 --> 00:48:56,683
Of what?

875
00:48:56,684 --> 00:48:59,019
I was the only person at school.

876
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:02,814
I was worried I'd become a suspect.

877
00:49:02,815 --> 00:49:03,898
It's not too late.

878
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:05,316
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

879
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:07,445
Tell me everything

880
00:49:08,195 --> 00:49:09,572
right from the beginning.

881
00:49:13,451 --> 00:49:18,079
At night, the student's mother turned up,
saying her daughter was missing.

882
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:19,915
SEVEN MONTHS AGO

883
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:23,127
[exclaims in horror]

884
00:49:23,961 --> 00:49:25,045
[sobbing]

885
00:49:25,588 --> 00:49:27,214
[security guard] <i>But she was dead.</i>

886
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:30,968
<i>The police came
and asked for the security footage,</i>

887
00:49:31,385 --> 00:49:32,553
<i>but the cameras were off.</i>

888
00:49:33,846 --> 00:49:34,972
So,

889
00:49:36,765 --> 00:49:38,058
I lied

890
00:49:39,143 --> 00:49:41,812
that they'd been down for a few days.

891
00:49:43,564 --> 00:49:45,191
But I thought it was a suicide.

892
00:49:46,066 --> 00:49:47,817
It's hard to say now.

893
00:49:47,818 --> 00:49:51,362
You said the cameras weren't down.
Someone turned them off.

894
00:49:51,363 --> 00:49:52,406
I mean,

895
00:49:53,532 --> 00:49:57,494
I don't know if they were turned off
or if I pressed the wrong button.

896
00:49:57,495 --> 00:50:00,122
I was still new to the job back then.

897
00:50:01,457 --> 00:50:02,749
I swear, no one was there.

898
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:05,461
When did you realize the cameras were off?

899
00:50:06,795 --> 00:50:10,298
I found out after the police arrived,
so it was near midnight.

900
00:50:10,299 --> 00:50:12,258
When did you last see them on?

901
00:50:12,259 --> 00:50:16,679
I went to do my rounds at 10:00 p.m.,
and they were working fine then.

902
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:19,182
[♪ music swells, fades]

903
00:50:19,183 --> 00:50:20,351
[sighs softly]

904
00:50:21,143 --> 00:50:23,103
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

905
00:50:32,446 --> 00:50:35,740
If someone turned off
the security cameras...

906
00:50:35,741 --> 00:50:38,202
Was Baek Yuna murdered?

907
00:50:39,203 --> 00:50:41,329
Any luck reaching Baek Yuna's parents?

908
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:44,416
No. They both moved abroad,
and I can't get a hold of them.

909
00:50:45,209 --> 00:50:46,627
[breathes deeply]

910
00:50:48,546 --> 00:50:50,755
Let's focus on Moon Seyeon's case first.

911
00:50:50,756 --> 00:50:51,757
Okay.

912
00:50:52,758 --> 00:50:56,303
But this seems like an accident,
not a crime.

913
00:50:57,471 --> 00:50:59,974
- We'll have to find out.
- How?

914
00:51:00,641 --> 00:51:02,308
- I know an expert.
- [♪ music fades]

915
00:51:02,309 --> 00:51:04,270
- Kyungjin, let's go.
- Okay.

916
00:51:08,023 --> 00:51:09,149
[door opens]

917
00:51:13,195 --> 00:51:14,947
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

918
00:51:16,323 --> 00:51:18,157
You're asking if this is a real curse?

919
00:51:18,158 --> 00:51:19,535
- Yes.
- Yes.

920
00:51:21,078 --> 00:51:22,496
- [shaman] Mmm.
- [bells jangling]

921
00:51:33,090 --> 00:51:34,424
[♪ music fades]

922
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:35,426
It's not.

923
00:51:36,176 --> 00:51:38,679
This poor child
is no longer in this world.

924
00:51:39,680 --> 00:51:41,181
She has already left.

925
00:51:41,765 --> 00:51:45,269
Ah. Then what about this student?

926
00:51:50,190 --> 00:51:51,400
Another one died?

927
00:51:52,026 --> 00:51:55,487
Yes, another student died
in the exact same place.

928
00:51:58,324 --> 00:51:59,491
[sighs deeply]

929
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:01,076
[bells jangling]

930
00:52:01,910 --> 00:52:03,954
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

931
00:52:13,297 --> 00:52:15,049
[screeching eerily]

932
00:52:17,635 --> 00:52:19,552
[♪ music swells]

933
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:20,803
[♪ music resumes tempo]

934
00:52:20,804 --> 00:52:22,680
She's still at the school.

935
00:52:22,681 --> 00:52:24,933
A vengeful spirit is there.

936
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:29,104
[grunts softly]

937
00:52:29,772 --> 00:52:31,231
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

938
00:52:36,820 --> 00:52:37,821
[spectral exhale]

939
00:52:42,201 --> 00:52:43,534
[spectral exhale]

940
00:52:43,535 --> 00:52:45,536
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music continues]

941
00:52:45,537 --> 00:52:46,872
- [shaman] What is that?
- [spectral exhale]

942
00:52:48,624 --> 00:52:50,000
[♪ music turns ominous]

943
00:52:51,126 --> 00:52:52,378
[♪ music swells]

944
00:52:54,922 --> 00:52:56,048
[♪ music fades]

945
00:52:57,716 --> 00:52:58,800
[exhales softly]

946
00:52:58,801 --> 00:53:00,343
What is it?

947
00:53:00,344 --> 00:53:03,221
An item with fur, about this big.

948
00:53:03,222 --> 00:53:04,597
She left it behind.

949
00:53:04,598 --> 00:53:05,641
[whispering] What could it be?

950
00:53:07,685 --> 00:53:09,395
Why is your mind so troubled?

951
00:53:10,145 --> 00:53:11,146
[chuckles]

952
00:53:11,772 --> 00:53:13,023
You got dumped by a girl.

953
00:53:14,274 --> 00:53:15,401
[Kyungjin gasps]

954
00:53:17,945 --> 00:53:18,946
How did you know?

955
00:53:19,571 --> 00:53:21,864
Call her. She's waiting for you.

956
00:53:21,865 --> 00:53:24,075
What? Right now?

957
00:53:24,076 --> 00:53:25,910
Are you going to let
a good woman get away?

958
00:53:25,911 --> 00:53:27,329
No.

959
00:53:30,624 --> 00:53:31,875
[Isoo chuckles]

960
00:53:32,584 --> 00:53:33,627
[shaman] Detective Jin.

961
00:53:34,586 --> 00:53:35,795
Yes?

962
00:53:35,796 --> 00:53:38,298
I have a feeling something bad
is going to happen soon.

963
00:53:39,925 --> 00:53:41,676
- To me?
- Yes.

964
00:53:41,677 --> 00:53:43,010
[♪ melancholy music playing]

965
00:53:43,011 --> 00:53:45,472
Misfortune and trouble
with the law await you.

966
00:53:46,140 --> 00:53:47,558
I see blood.

967
00:53:52,104 --> 00:53:53,105
Be careful.

968
00:53:53,814 --> 00:53:56,107
Someone is after you.

969
00:53:56,108 --> 00:53:58,569
You mustn't open the door.

970
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:04,742
[♪ music fades]

971
00:54:10,748 --> 00:54:12,833
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

972
00:54:36,190 --> 00:54:37,274
[exhales softly]

973
00:54:38,776 --> 00:54:39,943
[sighs heavily]

974
00:54:45,073 --> 00:54:46,241
[sighs softly]

975
00:54:47,409 --> 00:54:48,577
[grunts]

976
00:54:52,331 --> 00:54:54,291
[♪ pleasant music plays, fades]

977
00:55:00,589 --> 00:55:02,173
[birds chirping]

978
00:55:02,174 --> 00:55:03,300
[sighs softly]

979
00:55:14,603 --> 00:55:16,104
[♪ ominous music playing]

980
00:55:37,918 --> 00:55:39,795
[♪ ticking, ominous music playing]

981
00:55:46,218 --> 00:55:47,761
[♪ music swells]

982
00:55:53,141 --> 00:55:54,225
[♪ music fades]

983
00:55:54,226 --> 00:55:55,561
[cell phone vibrating]

984
00:55:56,144 --> 00:55:57,187
Mmm.

985
00:55:58,230 --> 00:55:59,690
- Hello?
- [Isoo] <i>Doctor.</i>

986
00:56:00,315 --> 00:56:03,110
I just woke up and my house is a wreck.

987
00:56:05,112 --> 00:56:07,322
[sighs] I don't remember anything
about this.

988
00:56:08,532 --> 00:56:11,534
Does the medication I'm on
have any side effects?

989
00:56:11,535 --> 00:56:14,579
[psychiatrist] <i>No, the medication
you're currently taking is very safe.</i>

990
00:56:14,580 --> 00:56:18,124
You might feel a little dizzy,
but there are no serious side effects.

991
00:56:18,125 --> 00:56:21,127
Could a burglar have broken in?

992
00:56:21,128 --> 00:56:23,839
No. No one can get in here.

993
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:26,091
And nothing's been stolen.

994
00:56:26,800 --> 00:56:29,344
- Would you like to come in to see me?
<i>- Yes, all right.</i>

995
00:56:30,929 --> 00:56:32,054
[line disconnects]

996
00:56:32,055 --> 00:56:33,515
[♪ ominous music playing]

997
00:56:37,728 --> 00:56:38,895
[♪ music fades]

998
00:56:42,316 --> 00:56:43,650
Hey, Detective Joo.

999
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:46,403
Have a look at this.

1000
00:56:47,112 --> 00:56:48,739
This red thing here.

1001
00:56:49,323 --> 00:56:50,406
It's a drug.

1002
00:56:50,407 --> 00:56:52,491
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1003
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:53,784
- A drug?
- Yes.

1004
00:56:53,785 --> 00:56:56,621
I've never seen it before.
Narcotics are looking into it.

1005
00:56:56,622 --> 00:56:58,624
- I'll let you know once I know more.
- Okay.

1006
00:56:59,249 --> 00:57:00,709
- Take care.
- Okay.

1007
00:57:06,173 --> 00:57:08,174
[line connects, ringing]

1008
00:57:08,175 --> 00:57:09,176
[Dr. Yoon] <i>Hello?</i>

1009
00:57:09,926 --> 00:57:12,261
That metabolite found
in Moon Seyeon's blood.

1010
00:57:12,262 --> 00:57:13,554
Ah.

1011
00:57:13,555 --> 00:57:15,097
The lab results came back.

1012
00:57:15,098 --> 00:57:17,516
- It's a drug.
- What kind of drug is it?

1013
00:57:17,517 --> 00:57:20,853
[sighs] <i>I think this is the first time
it's turned up in Korea.</i>

1014
00:57:20,854 --> 00:57:23,856
You know that case overseas
when someone was paralyzed

1015
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:26,233
- after touching a bill on the ground?
- Yes.

1016
00:57:26,234 --> 00:57:27,985
<i>It's a similar kind of drug.</i>

1017
00:57:27,986 --> 00:57:30,029
<i>It causes hallucinations in most people,</i>

1018
00:57:30,030 --> 00:57:33,574
but the victim had asthma,
so it triggered an attack.

1019
00:57:33,575 --> 00:57:34,743
[♪ music swells]

1020
00:57:37,162 --> 00:57:38,246
[♪ music fades]

1021
00:57:39,289 --> 00:57:40,624
There was a drug?

1022
00:57:41,541 --> 00:57:42,542
[Hyera] Yes.

1023
00:57:44,294 --> 00:57:46,712
Someone slipped this drug
into Seyeon's bag...

1024
00:57:46,713 --> 00:57:48,464
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

1025
00:57:48,465 --> 00:57:50,758
<i>...and it made her hallucinate.</i>

1026
00:57:50,759 --> 00:57:52,927
That triggered an asthma attack
and she died.

1027
00:57:52,928 --> 00:57:55,972
Did someone put this drug in to kill her?

1028
00:57:56,932 --> 00:57:59,226
It might have been
to take the lead role from her.

1029
00:58:00,477 --> 00:58:04,313
They might not have known
it was dangerous for someone with asthma.

1030
00:58:04,314 --> 00:58:07,400
They put a curse pouch in her bag?

1031
00:58:07,401 --> 00:58:09,193
It must've happened at school.

1032
00:58:09,194 --> 00:58:10,195
Yes.

1033
00:58:11,405 --> 00:58:13,447
The culprit would've left a trace.

1034
00:58:13,448 --> 00:58:14,990
- Call in a drug-sniffing dog.
- Got it.

1035
00:58:14,991 --> 00:58:15,992
[♪ music fades]

1036
00:58:30,799 --> 00:58:31,800
[bag unzips]

1037
00:58:34,594 --> 00:58:36,346
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1038
00:59:11,256 --> 00:59:13,049
[breathes heavily]

1039
00:59:14,968 --> 00:59:17,178
- [♪ ominous sting]
- [♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

1040
00:59:17,179 --> 00:59:18,346
[exhales shakily]

1041
00:59:18,764 --> 00:59:19,806
[Juhee] Good morning.

1042
00:59:22,058 --> 00:59:23,393
Is everyone here?

1043
00:59:26,605 --> 00:59:28,273
All right, get into formation.

1044
00:59:36,031 --> 00:59:37,908
[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

1045
00:59:41,244 --> 00:59:42,370
[brakes squeal]

1046
00:59:48,460 --> 00:59:49,919
All right.

1047
00:59:49,920 --> 00:59:51,086
Get ready!

1048
00:59:51,087 --> 00:59:52,297
[♪ music fades]

1049
00:59:56,259 --> 00:59:57,593
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1050
00:59:57,594 --> 00:59:59,012
[blade swooshing]

1051
01:00:10,774 --> 01:00:12,192
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1052
01:00:12,776 --> 01:00:14,027
[barking]

1053
01:00:18,615 --> 01:00:20,158
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1054
01:00:25,580 --> 01:00:28,124
[high-pitched tone droning, fades]

1055
01:00:30,710 --> 01:00:32,128
[blade swooshing]

1056
01:00:50,647 --> 01:00:52,440
[spectral breathing]

1057
01:00:55,068 --> 01:00:56,611
[♪ music swells]

1058
01:01:01,032 --> 01:01:02,575
[Gaeun panting]

1059
01:01:02,576 --> 01:01:03,659
[♪ music fades]

1060
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:05,744
[panting, breath trembling]

1061
01:01:05,745 --> 01:01:07,538
- [stick taps twice]
- What are you doing?

1062
01:01:07,539 --> 01:01:09,291
[Gaeun, breath trembling]

1063
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:12,293
Gaeun, what's wrong?

1064
01:01:12,294 --> 01:01:13,502
[breathing frantically]

1065
01:01:13,503 --> 01:01:14,712
[breathing slowing, trembling]

1066
01:01:14,713 --> 01:01:16,256
[♪ ominous music playing]

1067
01:01:17,465 --> 01:01:19,301
[spectral breathing]

1068
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:22,888
[Seyeon] <i>I'm the lead dancer.</i>

1069
01:01:26,182 --> 01:01:27,893
[slow, heavy, distorted breathing]

1070
01:01:40,989 --> 01:01:45,327
- [Yuna] <i>I'm the lead dancer.
-</i> [Seyeon] <i>I'm the lead dancer.</i>

1071
01:01:49,998 --> 01:01:51,875
[spectral murmuring]

1072
01:01:53,251 --> 01:01:55,337
[♪ music swells]

1073
01:01:58,048 --> 01:01:59,548
[distorted screaming]

1074
01:01:59,549 --> 01:02:00,966
[sharp swoosh, slash]

1075
01:02:00,967 --> 01:02:02,093
[♪ music slows]

1076
01:02:03,136 --> 01:02:04,971
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1077
01:02:06,890 --> 01:02:09,225
[Gaeun breathing heavily, distorted]

1078
01:02:16,274 --> 01:02:17,567
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1079
01:02:19,819 --> 01:02:21,446
[♪ music swells]

1080
01:02:24,240 --> 01:02:25,366
[♪ music fades]

1081
01:02:25,367 --> 01:02:26,450
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 9

1082
01:02:26,451 --> 01:02:28,035
WHAT'S THE TRUTH BEHIND THE CURSE?

1083
01:02:28,036 --> 01:02:30,038
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1084
01:02:45,553 --> 01:02:49,056
Special Cast. Joo Hyunyoung

1085
01:02:49,057 --> 01:02:52,477
Special Cast. Jeon Hyebin

1086
01:03:04,197 --> 01:03:05,698
A curse pouch had drugs inside.

1087
01:03:05,699 --> 01:03:08,242
[Juhee] <i>Are you saying one of my students
did something like that?</i>

1088
01:03:08,243 --> 01:03:09,493
Can we talk for a moment?

1089
01:03:09,494 --> 01:03:10,619
Where would I get drugs?

1090
01:03:10,620 --> 01:03:12,204
[Hyera] <i>Did you find anything
on Seyeon's phone?</i>

1091
01:03:12,205 --> 01:03:14,206
[shaman] <i>An item with fur, about this big.</i>

1092
01:03:14,207 --> 01:03:15,916
The shaman said she saw this.

1093
01:03:15,917 --> 01:03:17,835
This is a video app.

1094
01:03:17,836 --> 01:03:19,420
You can't do this.

1095
01:03:19,421 --> 01:03:21,797
- [students gasp]
- [Hayun] <i>I was only messing around.</i>

1096
01:03:21,798 --> 01:03:23,382
<i>But how did you know?</i>

1097
01:03:23,383 --> 01:03:24,550
Let's do this!

1098
01:03:24,551 --> 01:03:26,593
Did Isoo side with Joo Hyera?

1099
01:03:26,594 --> 01:03:28,220
[Minjae] <i>Yu Seongwon brought a woman over.</i>

1100
01:03:28,221 --> 01:03:30,723
- [Hyera] <i>We have no way of watching him.</i>
- [car horn honking]

1101
01:03:30,724 --> 01:03:32,641
What was the worst thing you've ever done?

1102
01:03:32,642 --> 01:03:33,726
What about you?

1103
01:03:33,727 --> 01:03:36,353
The worst thing I've done?

1104
01:03:36,354 --> 01:03:37,604
<i>You'd be shocked if you knew.</i>

1105
01:03:37,605 --> 01:03:39,189
<i>How do you want to die?</i>

1106
01:03:39,190 --> 01:03:40,525
[♪ music fades]

1107
01:03:44,154 --> 01:03:45,572
Why do you take photographs?

1108
01:03:46,656 --> 01:03:48,615
To feel you while I work.

1109
01:03:48,616 --> 01:03:49,908
[♪ foreboding music playing]

1110
01:03:49,909 --> 01:03:51,745
Can I get a copy if they come out well?

1111
01:03:53,079 --> 01:03:54,329
[chuckles softly]

1112
01:03:54,330 --> 01:03:55,331
No.

1113
01:03:58,334 --> 01:04:00,753
What kind of artwork
are you going to make me into?

1114
01:04:00,754 --> 01:04:02,838
I'm not sure. [sighs softly]

1115
01:04:02,839 --> 01:04:04,590
I can't say I know you yet.

1116
01:04:04,591 --> 01:04:06,008
What do you like most?

1117
01:04:06,009 --> 01:04:08,386
I like painting the most.

1118
01:04:09,888 --> 01:04:11,556
I wish I could

1119
01:04:12,348 --> 01:04:14,976
spend just one month painting,
without worrying about money.

1120
01:04:15,977 --> 01:04:17,062
[scoffs]

1121
01:04:18,063 --> 01:04:19,272
That's no fun.

1122
01:04:19,856 --> 01:04:21,399
What's no fun?

1123
01:04:28,073 --> 01:04:29,282
[exhales softly]

1124
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:32,077
Want a glass of champagne?

1125
01:04:32,786 --> 01:04:34,788
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
